    "issue_alignment": "The gitno buffer interface stores received socket data in a fixed 65536-byte region and only zeroes bytes beyond the current offset; a completely full buffer therefore provides no NUL terminator after a pkt payload. set_data() then applies unbounded C-string operations (strstr) to a pointer inside that payload, producing an out-of-bounds read."
